# O251 — the replay the open hands forward, measured
#
# Date        2026-09-22
# Tree        9774840 (O251 merged) vs a2e7892 (O250 merged, O251 absent)
# Corpus      a COPY of the o242-corpus volume — 102,360 drawers,
#             102,361 audit records, sealed. The reference volume is never
#             mutated; every run below is against the copy.
# Retrieval   UNDERCROFT_RETRIEVAL=pq. Measured without it first and the
#             search cost ~5,000 ms, in which an ~88 ms replay is invisible;
#             that first attempt is why this line exists.
# Instrument  `serve-http --read-only` — it replays to JUDGE the anchor and
#             declines to heal it, so the condition survives being observed.
#             A writable open heals, which is how an earlier version of this
#             probe destroyed its own premise.
#             Per sample: time the FIRST guarded search (floored `min_trust`,
#             so it consults a label) and a SECOND one. The second carries no
#             replay under either binary, so first-second isolates the replay.
# Control     The pre-fix binary is the POSITIVE CONTROL. It must read
#             chain_replays=1 on the lagging arm, or a zero elsewhere means
#             only that the probe never produced a lag.
#
# columns: open_ms first_ms second_ms chain_replays anchor_lag_reported
